\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{From a mass wall to a free boundary}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Kaplan places a step in the mass along an extra lattice
direction. The defect supports modes localized there
\citet{Eqs. (7)-(13), pp. 4-5}{kaplan1992method}.
Shamir imposes a free boundary in a fifth direction and
studies both a semi-infinite lattice and a finite slab
\citet{Sections 2-3}{shamir1993chiral}.
Golterman, Jansen and Kaplan obtain the alternating binomial
coefficient for odd bulk dimension in their comparison of
the Wilson current with the wall-mode count
\citet{Eqs. (9), (12), pp. 6-7}{golterman1993chern}.}

\p{For a finite slab the count in \ref{fdip-01AI} comes
from the transverse labels present on one face. Changing a
transverse period from odd to even adds the label #{\pi}
on that axis. It can change this count even when the projector
ranks at each existing corner stay fixed.}
